{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"operator verification and release safety","packet_sha256":"daa8d78a88ab7201a9a29877c96d58f4c1815f8b9c6f56cd303981efa217e7a5","reviewed_input_identity_sha256":"7f0311e26d5963157a9bc6ad5f0f3ecdf4c5c686849ce610b33c34380f04a82f","verdict":"block","target_observations":null,"findings":[{"id":"R1","severity":"high","summary":"Unresolved create recovery can ignore a corrupted started receipt and retry a provider create.","evidence":["issue_tracker_observation.py find_unresolved_create skips any started receipt for which _read_receipt returns None.","The documented contract says an incomplete or invalid observation is unresolved and must not be treated as a mutation-free history.","A crash or receipt corruption can therefore permit a second create without first establishing whether the original provider mutation occurred."],"action":"Fail closed on any matching malformed or hash-invalid started receipt: return an unresolved/refusal outcome requiring operator disposition or a new verified recovery path, rather than continuing to create."},{"id":"R2","severity":"medium","summary":"The freeze CLI hashes the draft before validating that the supplied path is repository-relative.","evidence":["goal_binding_freeze.py run_freeze calls sha256_file(repo_root / draft_arg) before build_binding validates draft_path.","An absolute path or traversal path can cause the CLI to read and hash a file outside the repository before refusing the binding.","The later path validation prevents writing a binding, but it does not prevent the out-of-scope read."],"action":"Validate and resolve the draft path against repo_root before reading it; reject absolute, traversal, and symlink-escaping paths before hashing."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"The supplied tests cover normal freeze success, typed input failures, immutable attempt reuse, and an os.link race.","bin":"real-gap","disposition":"Those tests do not exercise malformed matching receipts or out-of-repository draft paths, so they do not retire either finding."},{"concern":"Freeze approval and parent identity are supplied as CLI arguments rather than live provider reads.","bin":"defer","disposition":"The packet documents provider verification later in Goal Run establishment; this review does not treat that interface choice alone as a blocker without the omitted caller/adapter contract."}],"next_move":"Repair the fail-open observation recovery and prevalidate draft paths, then add focused regression tests before release approval.","non_claims":["No provider roundtrip, host exposure, or external issue-state verification was performed.","This review judges only the identity-checked inline payload, not the current workspace.","No claim is made about unreviewed files or the complete Goal Run implementation."]}
